# Supabase migrations — run them yourself

Whenever you add or change files under `supabase/migrations/`, **apply them to the linked remote project in the same turn**. Do not leave this for the user.

## How

From the repo root, prefer `.tools/supabase-go`, then `.tools/supabase`:

```bash
.tools/supabase-go db push --yes
```

If `.tools/supabase` is missing, use `.tools/supabase-go`. If `db push` fails because remote history has extra versions, apply the new `.sql` file and mark it applied:

```bash
.tools/supabase-go db query --linked --file supabase/migrations/<file>.sql
.tools/supabase-go migration repair --status applied <version>
```

## Also

- Bump `AppInfo.databaseSchemaVersion` when a new migration is added (already required by release docs).
- If CLI auth fails, say so clearly — do not skip the push silently.
